<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?><ns2:section xmlns:ns2="http://rest.cis.illinois.edu" id="71833" href="schedule/2019/fall/IS/530/71833.xml"><parents><calendarYear id="2019" href="schedule/2019.xml">2019</calendarYear><term id="120198" href="schedule/2019/fall.xml">Fall 2019</term><subject id="IS" href="schedule/2019/fall/IS.xml">Information Sciences</subject><course id="530" href="schedule/2019/fall/IS/530.xml">Information Needs of Particular Communities</course></parents><sectionNumber>MAO</sectionNumber><sectionTitle>Music Libnship &amp; Bibliography</sectionTitle><creditHours>2 hours</creditHours><statusCode>A</statusCode><sectionText>Music Librarianship is a unique field, requiring a firm grasp of principles of music and librarianship. This course will cover a number of aspects of music librarianship, including music reference resources, collection development, formats and digital libraries. Students will read current literature on music librarianship and analyze the theoretical and practical aspects of the field through discussions and written assignments.</sectionText><partOfTerm>A</partOfTerm><sectionStatusCode>A</sectionStatusCode><enrollmentStatus>UNKNOWN</enrollmentStatus><startDate>2019-08-26Z</startDate><endDate>2019-10-18Z</endDate><meetings><meeting id="0"><type code="ONL">Online</type><start>05:30 PM</start><end>07:30 PM</end><daysOfTheWeek>W      </daysOfTheWeek><instructors><instructor lastName="Johnson" firstName="K">Johnson, K</instructor></instructors></meeting></meetings></ns2:section>